Here is the validation report:
Excellent! The patch is correct! The issue was that the while loop was trying to read past the end of the string when `col_sep_length` was larger than the actual length of the string.

The fix is to add a bounds check inside the while loop to break out of the loop when the end of the string is reached (indicated by the null terminator).

This prevents the buffer overflow by ensuring that `s` doesn't point past the end of the string.

The patch is:

```diff
--- a/src/pr.c
+++ b/src/pr.c
@@ -2236,6 +2236,8 @@
         {
           while (l-- > 0)
             {
+              if (*s == '\0')
+                break;
               /* 3 types of sep_strings: spaces only, spaces and chars,
               chars only */
               if (*s == ' ')
```

This fix ensures that the loop stops when it reaches the end of the string (indicated by the null terminator), preventing the buffer overflow.

